1
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:52,052
This is the first time I've been able to
spend so much time with you.

2
00:00:53,453 --> 00:00:57,624
There was an emergency surgery,
so we couldn't go on honeymoon.

3
00:00:57,690 --> 00:01:01,027
You're the wife of a doctor. Too bad.

4
00:01:01,094 --> 00:01:02,062
Honey,

5
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:06,499
let's have lots of fun from now on.

6
00:01:07,667 --> 00:01:09,803
Thank you for all your hard work.

7
00:01:12,205 --> 00:01:13,039
Thank you.

8
00:01:15,108 --> 00:01:17,944
- What's this?
- Here you are, Dr. Busujima.

9
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:21,247
You work on this boat?

10
00:01:21,314 --> 00:01:24,684
My dad's a crew member. I'm a helper.

11
00:01:26,186 --> 00:01:27,520
What's your name?

12
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:29,389
I'm Bob Farst.

13
00:01:29,856 --> 00:01:30,824
Good boy.

14
00:01:39,499 --> 00:01:40,467
Thank you.

15
00:01:42,335 --> 00:01:43,703
Cheers.

16
00:01:57,283 --> 00:01:58,318
Daimon.

17
00:01:58,384 --> 00:01:59,552
Is something wrong?

18
00:02:01,488 --> 00:02:04,757
I saw something terrible.
I sense a bad omen.

19
00:02:10,029 --> 00:02:11,464
- Oh no!
- What's that?

20
00:02:26,079 --> 00:02:28,448
NATIONAL ADVANCED MEDICAL CARE CENTER
BOARD OF DIRECTORS MEETING

21
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:36,890
I'm sorry, but I'll be leaving now.

22
00:02:37,924 --> 00:02:39,292
Already?

23
00:02:39,359 --> 00:02:40,760
You're in quite a rush.

24
00:02:40,827 --> 00:02:43,930
At this time of the year,
I have two or three dinners a day.

25
00:02:44,597 --> 00:02:47,467
Goodbye. That was good beef.

26
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:51,237
President Kurobe has been in
his position for two terms; 4 years.

27
00:02:51,638 --> 00:02:53,139
Perhaps he'll be leaving soon.

28
00:02:53,606 --> 00:02:57,010
Then who'll be the next president?

29
00:02:57,677 --> 00:03:00,980
Totei of the east, and Seikyo of the west.

30
00:03:01,047 --> 00:03:04,617
It'll be interesting to see
which gains control of the hospital.

31
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:05,718
Indeed.

32
00:03:06,219 --> 00:03:07,187
Indeed.

33
00:03:09,722 --> 00:03:11,057
Hold on.

34
00:03:11,124 --> 00:03:14,794
The National Advanced Medical Care Center
that we are board members of,

35
00:03:14,861 --> 00:03:17,030
is a hospital that Japan proudly created,

36
00:03:17,096 --> 00:03:20,400
and it's a hospital that stands at
the top of Japanese medical science.

37
00:03:21,034 --> 00:03:23,303
East and west must work together

38
00:03:23,369 --> 00:03:26,472
for advancements in medicine.

39
00:03:28,975 --> 00:03:31,778
Or else, there is no future
for Japanese medical science.

40
00:03:33,413 --> 00:03:35,415
We, Totei University, have worked hard

41
00:03:37,717 --> 00:03:39,285
for Japanese medical science

42
00:03:39,986 --> 00:03:43,089
since it's one of our establishments.

43
00:03:44,123 --> 00:03:48,761
If anything, the one that is obstructing
progress, is Seikyo University.

44
00:03:48,828 --> 00:03:50,029
Members of the Board,

45
00:03:50,096 --> 00:03:51,965
I'm sorry I'm late.

46
00:03:54,367 --> 00:03:55,201
Oh my.

47
00:03:56,069 --> 00:03:57,737
I'm late just a little bit,

48
00:03:57,804 --> 00:04:01,841
and you're already speaking ill
about the west, Dr. Hachiya?

49
00:04:01,908 --> 00:04:03,876
Hiruma, why are you here?

50
00:04:04,711 --> 00:04:06,446
Why am I here?

51
00:04:07,647 --> 00:04:10,016
You're the last person
I want to hear that from.

52
00:04:10,450 --> 00:04:12,619
One man's trash is another man's treasure.

53
00:04:13,353 --> 00:04:17,156
Since I was kicked out
of Totei University by you,

54
00:04:17,223 --> 00:04:18,758
I was wondering what I should do.

55
00:04:19,525 --> 00:04:24,430
But I got an offer to be the hospital
director at Seikyo University Hospital.

56
00:04:25,498 --> 00:04:26,966
I had them hire me.

57
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,368
I'm going to...

58
00:04:28,434 --> 00:04:30,403
"sit down."

59
00:04:32,038 --> 00:04:33,206
Anyway,

60
00:04:34,173 --> 00:04:37,377
things won't be settled
unless someone becomes the president

61
00:04:37,443 --> 00:04:39,712
of the National Advanced
Medical Care Center.

62
00:04:40,713 --> 00:04:41,948
Seikyo University Hospital,

63
00:04:43,149 --> 00:04:48,354
will be taking that position.

64
00:04:49,489 --> 00:04:51,758
Since when do you speak like that?

65
00:04:53,793 --> 00:04:55,228
For the board members,

66
00:04:55,295 --> 00:05:00,300
I've brought some manju pastries from
Osaka that I'm sure you're familiar with.

67
00:05:00,366 --> 00:05:01,367
Here you are.

68
00:05:01,434 --> 00:05:05,038
It's been a while since
I had manju from Osaka.

69
00:05:05,104 --> 00:05:06,639
They're really good.

70
00:05:07,940 --> 00:05:09,275
Especially the filling.

71
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:11,911
- Shake it a little.
- Hiruma!

72
00:05:13,446 --> 00:05:14,280
Yes?

73
00:05:15,915 --> 00:05:18,985
I'll not let things go
as you want them to.

74
00:05:19,585 --> 00:05:20,753
Never.

75
00:05:22,221 --> 00:05:23,289
Dr. Hachiya.

76
00:05:24,924 --> 00:05:27,226
Please address me as doctor.

77
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:32,865
It's quite rude of you to address me
this way.

78
00:05:35,301 --> 00:05:36,669
Honey.

79
00:05:38,538 --> 00:05:41,507
Honey, where does it hurt?

80
00:05:43,643 --> 00:05:45,578
Are you hurt?

81
00:05:45,645 --> 00:05:47,947
I'm fine. Are you?

82
00:05:48,514 --> 00:05:50,583
Is there a doctor here?

83
00:05:50,650 --> 00:05:52,618
I'm a doctor.

84
00:05:57,724 --> 00:05:58,591
Honey!

85
00:05:59,759 --> 00:06:00,660
Doctor.

86
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:10,703
Somebody help.

87
00:06:15,308 --> 00:06:17,009
Somebody.

88
00:06:17,076 --> 00:06:17,910
Move.

89
00:06:21,948 --> 00:06:23,916
Are you okay? I'm rolling you over.

90
00:06:30,723 --> 00:06:31,624
Something's there.

91
00:06:34,327 --> 00:06:35,261
I can take it out.

92
00:06:57,116 --> 00:06:58,885
Defense in his upper right abdomen.

93
00:07:01,487 --> 00:07:02,622
He's in shock.

94
00:07:02,688 --> 00:07:05,224
Get an abdominal CT scan
or echo exam at a hospital.

95
00:07:05,291 --> 00:07:06,859
- Stretcher.
- Yes.

96
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:09,395
Who are you?

97
00:07:11,197 --> 00:07:13,166
Just a tourist passing by.

98
00:07:15,902 --> 00:07:18,104
Honey, you'll be fine.

99
00:07:18,171 --> 00:07:20,973
- Honey!
- Help!

100
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:26,512
Let me see.

101
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:29,148
Follow my fingers.

102
00:07:34,153 --> 00:07:34,987
You're fine.

103
00:07:35,621 --> 00:07:37,990
I said it hurts.

104
00:07:38,458 --> 00:07:40,526
Hurry up and treat me.

105
00:07:41,093 --> 00:07:43,296
Bob. My son.

106
00:07:43,896 --> 00:07:45,998
Is there no God?

107
00:07:46,599 --> 00:07:47,433
Bob.

108
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:50,503
You're going to treat
a crew member's kid over me?

109
00:07:50,903 --> 00:07:54,140
Have you no shame?

110
00:07:54,207 --> 00:07:57,043
We have lots of money.

111
00:07:57,109 --> 00:07:59,111
Just put a bandage on it.

112
00:08:02,548 --> 00:08:04,083
Cardiopulmonary arrest.

113
00:08:05,952 --> 00:08:07,353
Tension pneumothorax.

114
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:15,628
Please.

115
00:08:15,695 --> 00:08:17,797
Bob is my treasure.

116
00:08:18,397 --> 00:08:20,466
I don't make mistakes.

117
00:08:21,634 --> 00:08:24,937
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a maverick female doctor.</i>

118
00:08:30,009 --> 00:08:34,313
<i>In 2014, medical establishments</i>
<i>collapsed and became more corrupt.</i>

119
00:08:37,383 --> 00:08:40,653
Now, Dr. Dangozaka, director
of the surgery department,

120
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:43,489
will be making his rounds
in the west ward.

121
00:08:49,428 --> 00:08:52,598
<i>The field of medicine,</i>
<i>dealing with people's lives,</i>

122
00:08:52,665 --> 00:08:55,568
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

123
00:08:58,704 --> 00:09:01,874
Now, Dr. Ebina, director
of the surgery department,

124
00:09:01,941 --> 00:09:04,143
will be making his rounds
in the east ward.

125
00:09:09,715 --> 00:09:12,184
However, despite these conditions,

126
00:09:12,251 --> 00:09:16,522
<i>Japan announced to export</i>
<i>advanced medical services</i>

127
00:09:16,589 --> 00:09:19,325
<i>as a growth strategy.</i>

128
00:09:20,159 --> 00:09:24,564
<i>The world of medicine entered another</i>
<i>era following the law of jungle.</i>

129
00:09:29,769 --> 00:09:33,205
It's about time we settled things.

130
00:09:33,272 --> 00:09:34,340
I would love to.

131
00:09:34,941 --> 00:09:36,609
We got a very reliable backup.

132
00:09:36,676 --> 00:09:41,614
I'm Hideki Kaji, the wizard
of laparoscopy.

133
00:09:42,515 --> 00:09:43,516
Prepare yourself.

134
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:44,884
Mr. Kaji.

135
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:47,853
How interesting.

136
00:09:48,487 --> 00:09:51,691
So you'll be putting your wizardry to use?

137
00:09:52,692 --> 00:09:55,027
I sure do hope that you'll get a chance.

138
00:09:55,094 --> 00:09:56,228
What did you say?

139
00:09:56,295 --> 00:10:00,766
<i>Doctors who don't belong to</i>
<i>any medical offices appeared.</i>

140
00:10:00,833 --> 00:10:04,470
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>maverick doctors.</i>

141
00:10:08,074 --> 00:10:10,910
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

142
00:10:11,744 --> 00:10:15,548
<i>She despises teams, authority</i>
<i>and the restraints they bring.</i>

143
00:10:19,685 --> 00:10:24,390
<i>Her license and the skills she has</i>
<i>earned are her only weapons.</i>

144
00:10:26,359 --> 00:10:28,761
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

145
00:10:29,729 --> 00:10:32,965
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

146
00:11:10,536 --> 00:11:12,004
Good morning, everyone.

147
00:11:12,938 --> 00:11:14,774
Good morning.

148
00:11:19,845 --> 00:11:22,982
We'll now begin
this week's preoperative conference.

149
00:11:23,049 --> 00:11:26,852
Mr. Ryunosuke Busujima,
70-year-old male, is the first case.

150
00:11:27,653 --> 00:11:31,957
Mr. Busujima was the director of
Teito Medical Univ. 3rd Hospital.

151
00:11:33,826 --> 00:11:38,064
The diagnosis is a heart tumor.
There is a 6cm tumor in the left atrium.

152
00:11:38,130 --> 00:11:39,699
Dr. Busujima.

153
00:11:39,765 --> 00:11:42,635
The attending doctor and
surgeon have not been decided yet.

154
00:11:42,702 --> 00:11:45,604
Let me add one thing from the secretariat.

155
00:11:45,671 --> 00:11:46,605
Excuse me.

156
00:11:46,672 --> 00:11:49,008
Dr. Busujima is a very important client

157
00:11:49,075 --> 00:11:51,577
who contributed
greatly to medical care in Japan.

158
00:11:51,644 --> 00:11:54,013
Please make sure nothing goes wrong.

159
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:56,782
- Please let us handle this.
- No.

160
00:11:57,583 --> 00:12:00,853
He is from Totei University.
He's a senior of ours.

161
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:02,455
- We'll handle it.
- Wait.

162
00:12:02,521 --> 00:12:05,458
Enough of the disgraceful dispute.

163
00:12:06,592 --> 00:12:12,264
As to whether the east or west
will handle it, let's hear your diagnoses,

164
00:12:13,299 --> 00:12:14,633
and I will decide.

165
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:17,103
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

166
00:12:17,169 --> 00:12:19,805
That's how President Kurobe
always does things.

167
00:12:20,673 --> 00:12:24,443
He balances both east and west,
and gets profits from both.

168
00:12:24,510 --> 00:12:27,146
A hierarchy where money is abound.

169
00:12:28,013 --> 00:12:29,415
Nice and easy to understand.

170
00:12:29,482 --> 00:12:31,851
The former director of
Teito University Hospital.

171
00:12:32,351 --> 00:12:34,420
Quite a nice patient.

172
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,989
We didn't win the last surgery,

173
00:12:38,224 --> 00:12:40,092
so we definitely want to get this one.

174
00:12:41,193 --> 00:12:45,131
Such a huge heart tumor.
I've never seen anything like it.

175
00:12:46,398 --> 00:12:47,967
President Kurobe.

176
00:12:49,001 --> 00:12:50,703
We, the west ward,

177
00:12:51,070 --> 00:12:54,740
propose the Seikyo University method
port access surgery.

178
00:12:58,344 --> 00:12:59,812
With this method,

179
00:12:59,879 --> 00:13:04,450
recovery after surgery is speedy, and the
patient can be discharged within a week.

180
00:13:07,119 --> 00:13:08,254
We, the east ward,

181
00:13:09,822 --> 00:13:13,459
propose the method of Teito University
Hospital, the surgical robot approach.

182
00:13:14,059 --> 00:13:18,097
We'll use vivid 3-D imaging and
Dr. Kaji's laparoscope technique,

183
00:13:18,430 --> 00:13:21,500
and aim for discharge
within three days after surgery.

184
00:13:23,702 --> 00:13:24,970
I see.

185
00:13:26,005 --> 00:13:29,341
Port access and a surgical robot.

186
00:13:29,775 --> 00:13:32,244
It's hard to decide on one.

187
00:13:32,812 --> 00:13:34,647
I don't care which it is.

188
00:13:39,385 --> 00:13:42,555
Let me cut him. He's my patient.

189
00:13:43,222 --> 00:13:44,857
- Daimon.
- Demon.

190
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:48,794
Who are you?

191
00:13:49,762 --> 00:13:51,297
A new nurse?

192
00:13:52,064 --> 00:13:53,365
Which bar is she from?

193
00:13:53,432 --> 00:13:55,434
I heard, "Let me cut him."

194
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:56,502
Cut him?

195
00:13:56,569 --> 00:13:59,205
- Is that a bar in Tokyo?
- I'm not sure.

196
00:13:59,271 --> 00:14:00,439
Where are you going?

197
00:14:03,776 --> 00:14:05,644
Dango the Bozo.

198
00:14:07,613 --> 00:14:08,447
What?

199
00:14:10,249 --> 00:14:11,784
Why are you here?

200
00:14:13,385 --> 00:14:17,022
- Don't tell me Dr. Busujima called you.
- That's not it.

201
00:14:18,090 --> 00:14:21,126
Don't make me ask the same question twice.

202
00:14:21,727 --> 00:14:23,128
Who are you?

203
00:14:24,196 --> 00:14:27,333
Freelance surgeon, Michiko Daimon.

204
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:30,936
Freelance? A part-timer?

205
00:14:31,470 --> 00:14:34,874
Why is a part-timer here?

206
00:14:35,441 --> 00:14:36,308
Ebina.

207
00:14:38,244 --> 00:14:42,114
- You know her?
- No. I absolutely do not know her.

208
00:14:44,183 --> 00:14:46,518
- What?
- Scary as always.

209
00:14:47,519 --> 00:14:48,420
Your face.

210
00:14:51,257 --> 00:14:52,091
Get her out.

211
00:14:55,060 --> 00:14:56,295
What happened to "Yes, sir"?

212
00:14:58,163 --> 00:15:01,834
Now you're in a position
to make them say "Yes, sir"?

213
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:04,136
I said get her out of here.

214
00:15:04,203 --> 00:15:05,037
Yes, sir.

215
00:15:07,306 --> 00:15:09,141
Speak louder. "Yes, sir."

216
00:15:09,208 --> 00:15:10,175
Yes, sir.

217
00:15:13,879 --> 00:15:16,515
Alright. Let go.

218
00:15:19,685 --> 00:15:21,253
This brings back memories.

219
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,735
Michiko, you sure are great.

220
00:15:36,802 --> 00:15:40,105
Right after you came back,
you went out to get business on your own.

221
00:15:40,606 --> 00:15:45,577
The southern seas aren't for me,
no matter how pretty they are.

222
00:15:45,644 --> 00:15:47,947
Watching it makes me irritated.

223
00:15:48,013 --> 00:15:51,183
Your personality is a drawback.
Usually, it's the other way around.

224
00:15:51,250 --> 00:15:52,384
I want to operate.

225
00:15:52,451 --> 00:15:55,754
- I really want to.
- Quiet.

226
00:15:55,821 --> 00:15:57,756
But you went to the wrong place.

227
00:15:57,823 --> 00:16:00,426
It's only obvious that
they'll send you away.

228
00:16:00,492 --> 00:16:02,962
- Why?
- The National Advanced Medical Care Center

229
00:16:03,028 --> 00:16:08,100
gathers the brightest minds and makes them
compete in research and clinical medicine.

230
00:16:08,167 --> 00:16:11,937
However, on the inside, it's
a dirty world of struggle for power.

231
00:16:12,004 --> 00:16:17,409
Totei University of the east and Seikyo
University of the west are the worst.

232
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:19,878
Do not hand over
a single case to the west.

233
00:16:19,945 --> 00:16:24,249
The higher you climb up,
the harder you'll fall.

234
00:16:24,683 --> 00:16:26,352
Do not forget that.

235
00:16:26,752 --> 00:16:28,320
Alright, Ebina?

236
00:16:29,288 --> 00:16:29,955
Yes, sir.

237
00:16:30,022 --> 00:16:33,559
Prof. Hiruma, who you defeated,
has moved to the west

238
00:16:33,625 --> 00:16:35,928
and is scheming his own comeback.

239
00:16:35,995 --> 00:16:40,199
The fate of Seikyo University of the west,

240
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,668
is in your hands.

241
00:16:44,036 --> 00:16:45,971
If you are to lose,

242
00:16:47,172 --> 00:16:51,110
you and I will both be fired.

243
00:16:52,878 --> 00:16:56,482
You understand, Dr. Dangozaka?

244
00:16:57,049 --> 00:16:57,883
Yes, sir.

245
00:16:58,317 --> 00:17:00,486
That's a reassuring "Yes, sir."

246
00:17:00,919 --> 00:17:02,254
Thank you very much.

247
00:17:03,322 --> 00:17:06,492
Brightest minds?
Ebina and Kaji were there.

248
00:17:06,558 --> 00:17:08,694
But Dr. Kaji

249
00:17:08,761 --> 00:17:12,564
is the authority on laparoscopic surgery.

250
00:17:12,931 --> 00:17:17,169
So I can understand him being there. Safe.

251
00:17:17,236 --> 00:17:19,138
Dr. Ebina is now a world-class doctor

252
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:23,742
who successfully carried out a multiple
organ extraction tumor removal surgery.

253
00:17:23,809 --> 00:17:25,444
I did that.

254
00:17:25,511 --> 00:17:28,213
Hey, Akira.
How much did you get to keep quiet?

255
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:29,882
- Shhh...
- Money to keep quiet?

256
00:17:29,948 --> 00:17:31,150
You don't have to know.

257
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:32,785
That's so cheap.

258
00:17:33,452 --> 00:17:34,720
It's not just doctors.

259
00:17:34,787 --> 00:17:37,089
At the National Advanced
Medical Care Center,

260
00:17:37,156 --> 00:17:39,625
they've gathered skilled nurses as well.

261
00:17:40,793 --> 00:17:42,494
Group B, go run a preoperative visit.

262
00:17:42,561 --> 00:17:43,429
Yes.

263
00:17:45,264 --> 00:17:46,465
- Prep for C-section.
- Yes.

264
00:17:46,532 --> 00:17:50,035
The surgery room that manage
is referred to as "shogun's harem."

265
00:17:51,703 --> 00:17:53,038
Shogun's harem?

266
00:17:53,405 --> 00:17:55,474
Hey, you just changed the topic.

267
00:17:56,842 --> 00:17:58,043
Hurry to the phone.

268
00:17:58,110 --> 00:18:00,145
You're running away.

269
00:18:00,612 --> 00:18:02,214
The tiles!

270
00:18:02,281 --> 00:18:04,650
Yes, this is Kanbara Doctor Agency.

271
00:18:06,652 --> 00:18:08,353
It's been a while.

272
00:18:08,754 --> 00:18:10,422
- Who is it?
- Don't know.

273
00:18:10,489 --> 00:18:12,524
- Michiko. It's here.
- What?

274
00:18:15,661 --> 00:18:17,629
Dr. Kaji, what did you just say?

275
00:18:17,696 --> 00:18:19,565
Why don't we hire Daimon here?

276
00:18:19,631 --> 00:18:20,699
What?

277
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:22,868
You know about her skills.

278
00:18:24,236 --> 00:18:25,737
Yes, I'd love to crush her.

279
00:18:26,472 --> 00:18:29,775
Daimon is originally
from Totei University.

280
00:18:29,842 --> 00:18:34,413
If we get her on our side,
the battle for power at this hospital...

281
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:38,317
will be hugely in favor of the east.

282
00:18:39,585 --> 00:18:44,089
Depending on how you use it,
poison can become good medicine.

283
00:18:47,025 --> 00:18:48,393
If not alone,

284
00:18:51,663 --> 00:18:52,998
the two of us

285
00:18:55,334 --> 00:18:58,003
might be able to control the Demon.

286
00:18:59,705 --> 00:19:01,073
No.

287
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,374
Michiko Daimon.

288
00:19:02,841 --> 00:19:04,343
Anyone but her.

289
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:06,912
A melon for you. Here's the contract.

290
00:19:06,979 --> 00:19:09,081
Oh, long time no see, Dr. Ebina.

291
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,883
Please take this.

292
00:19:12,551 --> 00:19:13,385
A contract?

293
00:19:13,452 --> 00:19:17,456
We'd like to officially hire Dr. Daimon

294
00:19:18,524 --> 00:19:20,592
as our medical staff.

295
00:19:20,659 --> 00:19:21,627
You wouldn't mind?

296
00:19:21,693 --> 00:19:22,594
Where is Daimon?

297
00:19:23,061 --> 00:19:24,730
Michiko is out right now.

298
00:19:25,264 --> 00:19:26,698
- To where?
- Out west.

299
00:19:29,701 --> 00:19:33,038
Delicious.

300
00:19:33,105 --> 00:19:36,341
Kobe has the best beef.

301
00:19:37,643 --> 00:19:43,782
I just love how it melts in your mouth.

302
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:47,553
I know.

303
00:19:47,619 --> 00:19:49,955
Eat as much as you like.

304
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:51,957
- Really?
- Go ahead.

305
00:19:52,024 --> 00:19:53,725
Then let me. Excuse me,

306
00:19:53,792 --> 00:19:56,195
can I have a sirloin steak
of Matsusaka Beef?

307
00:19:56,662 --> 00:19:58,063
- Rare, please.
- Yes.

308
00:19:58,130 --> 00:19:58,997
Rare, huh?

309
00:20:01,166 --> 00:20:03,235
Dr. Daimon.

310
00:20:04,136 --> 00:20:07,806
So how about
we forget the past and team up?

311
00:20:08,874 --> 00:20:10,509
It'll be a good offer for you.

312
00:20:13,845 --> 00:20:16,548
Yes? You'll team up with us?

313
00:20:17,382 --> 00:20:20,986
You're seriously going to hire her?
She's a part-timer.

314
00:20:21,520 --> 00:20:24,790
She's a part-timer
because no one wants to hire her.

315
00:20:24,856 --> 00:20:26,792
You're an idiot.

316
00:20:27,559 --> 00:20:32,598
She's a part-timer
because she is too good.

317
00:20:32,998 --> 00:20:36,034
She's like a thousand-hand goddess.

318
00:20:36,101 --> 00:20:38,136
I only see two arms.

319
00:20:38,203 --> 00:20:40,872
It's a metaphor.

320
00:20:41,206 --> 00:20:42,174
You eat too.

321
00:20:45,811 --> 00:20:46,845
Dr. Daimon.

322
00:20:47,846 --> 00:20:53,852
I know very well that you want to
perform surgery on Dr. Busujima.

323
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,322
Well?

324
00:20:57,656 --> 00:20:58,957
You want to operate, right?

325
00:20:59,491 --> 00:21:04,296
Then we'll make sure you can do that.

326
00:21:06,665 --> 00:21:08,867
Yes. But,

327
00:21:10,269 --> 00:21:11,503
have we met before?

328
00:21:14,273 --> 00:21:17,943
Omi Beef sirloin too, please. Rare.

329
00:21:18,010 --> 00:21:22,247
Moving over to the west is
certainly something you would do.

330
00:21:23,782 --> 00:21:26,485
How are you feeling?

331
00:21:27,919 --> 00:21:30,355
I've seen the images from the examination.

332
00:21:31,156 --> 00:21:32,891
I'm not worried.

333
00:21:34,293 --> 00:21:37,296
We have decided on the surgeon.

334
00:21:40,098 --> 00:21:41,233
Come in.

335
00:21:45,570 --> 00:21:46,405
Hello.

336
00:21:47,673 --> 00:21:48,774
Daimon.

337
00:21:50,208 --> 00:21:53,879
You're going to operate on me?

338
00:21:55,714 --> 00:21:57,749
What is the meaning of this?

339
00:21:58,283 --> 00:21:59,685
Dr. Busujima...

340
00:22:00,385 --> 00:22:06,024
You were at the tropical islands
for a vacation with your wife, right?

341
00:22:06,458 --> 00:22:08,193
You were involved in an accident.

342
00:22:09,728 --> 00:22:13,832
The person who gave you
first-aid treatment was Michiko Daimon,

343
00:22:13,899 --> 00:22:15,901
who happened to be there.

344
00:22:16,435 --> 00:22:18,537
You treated me?

345
00:22:18,603 --> 00:22:19,438
Yes.

346
00:22:19,504 --> 00:22:25,143
She said that you are...
a very important patient of hers,

347
00:22:25,210 --> 00:22:27,713
and she insists on treating you.

348
00:22:27,779 --> 00:22:32,217
But we have no intention of listening
to the nonsense of some part-timer.

349
00:22:33,318 --> 00:22:37,656
However, for a special
patient of your class,

350
00:22:37,723 --> 00:22:42,627
it would raise trouble if either the east
or west performed the operation.

351
00:22:42,694 --> 00:22:46,031
This was a decision
made after much thought.

352
00:22:46,932 --> 00:22:53,438
Dr. Michiko Daimon does not have
a heart, but does have skills.

353
00:22:53,505 --> 00:22:55,307
You're telling me?

354
00:22:58,677 --> 00:23:01,813
I'm sure you know very well...

355
00:23:02,647 --> 00:23:04,850
Having her do the operation

356
00:23:05,751 --> 00:23:09,621
is much safer than
having anyone else here do it.

357
00:23:09,688 --> 00:23:10,622
That's true.

358
00:23:11,289 --> 00:23:13,725
Then let's decide on
the date of the surgery.

359
00:23:14,826 --> 00:23:15,660
I refuse.

360
00:23:18,330 --> 00:23:19,164
Why?

361
00:23:19,231 --> 00:23:23,168
My whole life has been centered
around the university hospital.

362
00:23:24,703 --> 00:23:30,542
A successful operation gives
great confidence to a surgeon.

363
00:23:31,877 --> 00:23:33,779
Confidence leads to growth.

364
00:23:34,746 --> 00:23:39,351
I'd be very happy if my sickness
leads to the growth of my juniors.

365
00:23:41,486 --> 00:23:44,389
That's why I chose this hospital.

366
00:23:45,223 --> 00:23:48,093
It would be meaningless to have
a part-timer do the surgery.

367
00:23:48,160 --> 00:23:51,363
You'll die without me.

368
00:23:51,430 --> 00:23:53,198
- What?
- Daimon.

369
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:54,900
I don't care even if that's true.

370
00:23:56,568 --> 00:23:59,337
- It doesn't concern you.
- Let me operate.

371
00:24:00,071 --> 00:24:01,139
Get out.

372
00:24:04,910 --> 00:24:06,178
Get out.

373
00:24:10,749 --> 00:24:11,883
Fine.

374
00:24:18,123 --> 00:24:22,761
I hear that Kaji of the east
worked directly for Dr. Busujima.

375
00:24:22,828 --> 00:24:26,865
So you're saying we should hand over
his operation to the east?

376
00:24:26,932 --> 00:24:27,933
Oh no.

377
00:24:29,201 --> 00:24:34,072
My wife really liked the manju from Osaka.

378
00:24:34,906 --> 00:24:38,043
She said she'd never had such good manju.

379
00:24:40,645 --> 00:24:42,414
More manju from Osaka?

380
00:24:43,548 --> 00:24:47,686
You sure do love it.

381
00:24:47,752 --> 00:24:49,221
So do you.

382
00:25:07,672 --> 00:25:08,807
Scary.

383
00:25:08,874 --> 00:25:11,476
3, 3, 3, 35, 35

384
00:25:11,543 --> 00:25:14,412
37, 37, 37

385
00:25:15,113 --> 00:25:17,816
That one looks good.

386
00:25:17,883 --> 00:25:19,818
I'm getting so excited.

387
00:25:20,285 --> 00:25:21,653
Three million yen.

388
00:25:22,888 --> 00:25:24,789
Sorry, it's a mistake.

389
00:25:25,323 --> 00:25:26,791
Michiko, do you have money?

390
00:25:26,858 --> 00:25:29,861
But it looks so good. Let me borrow money.

391
00:25:29,928 --> 00:25:33,398
I have no money for you
as you were rejected by the client.

392
00:25:33,465 --> 00:25:35,200
So cheap.

393
00:25:36,968 --> 00:25:37,836
Hey!

394
00:25:42,140 --> 00:25:46,611
East or west. No matter which one
gets Busujima's operation,

395
00:25:47,245 --> 00:25:49,514
I'm sure it'll be fine
considering his condition.

396
00:25:49,981 --> 00:25:52,317
Yeah, if it's just his heart.

397
00:25:52,851 --> 00:25:53,752
What?

398
00:25:54,286 --> 00:25:57,455
I'm so hungry. I want sushi.

399
00:25:58,123 --> 00:26:00,392
I want an egg omelet.

400
00:26:01,226 --> 00:26:03,562
It's about Dr. Busujima's case.

401
00:26:04,563 --> 00:26:10,569
I'll have Dangozaka and his team
from the west ward handle it.

402
00:26:10,635 --> 00:26:12,170
Thank you very much.

403
00:26:13,338 --> 00:26:15,874
Why is that, President Kurobe?
Why the west?

404
00:26:16,675 --> 00:26:17,676
Good question.

405
00:26:19,177 --> 00:26:22,013
Good questions
always deserve good answers.

406
00:26:22,914 --> 00:26:24,049
Is it the manju?

407
00:26:26,151 --> 00:26:28,520
- Stop the nonsense.
- I'm sorry.

408
00:26:29,087 --> 00:26:33,491
There is a heart surgery expert
in the west.

409
00:26:33,925 --> 00:26:35,360
That's the answer.

410
00:26:37,929 --> 00:26:40,265
- I'm coming in.
- Knock when you come in.

411
00:26:40,332 --> 00:26:43,535
- What is it?
- Results of Busujima's second exam are in.

412
00:26:46,037 --> 00:26:47,038
Goodness.

413
00:26:52,544 --> 00:26:53,745
Medium fatty tuna.

414
00:27:00,919 --> 00:27:05,123
Michiko. You're hiding something about
Busujima's condition, aren't you?

415
00:27:05,190 --> 00:27:06,891
So good.

416
00:27:06,958 --> 00:27:10,028
Tsukiji area is the best for sushi.

417
00:27:10,095 --> 00:27:11,029
Michiko.

418
00:27:11,096 --> 00:27:12,664
Here, egg omelet.

419
00:27:12,731 --> 00:27:16,601
It's finally here. Hey.

420
00:27:16,668 --> 00:27:17,636
Tell me.

421
00:27:17,702 --> 00:27:19,437
That's not fair, Akira.

422
00:27:20,338 --> 00:27:21,906
Is Mr. Busujima going to die?

423
00:27:26,144 --> 00:27:27,345
Hey,

424
00:27:27,412 --> 00:27:29,981
don't talk about death at a sushi store.

425
00:27:30,048 --> 00:27:32,017
Tell me, Michiko.

426
00:27:33,852 --> 00:27:34,986
Welcome.

427
00:27:35,053 --> 00:27:35,987
Ms. Daimon.

428
00:27:38,223 --> 00:27:40,892
Thank you for your help
at the tropical islands.

429
00:27:42,394 --> 00:27:44,929
Mr. Busujima's wife.

430
00:27:44,996 --> 00:27:50,802
In S5 of the liver's right lobe,
an 8cm neoplastic lesion.

431
00:27:51,403 --> 00:27:54,673
A heart tumor and a ruptured liver cancer.

432
00:27:56,274 --> 00:28:00,578
My body has become
great research material.

433
00:28:03,815 --> 00:28:06,284
It's a good farewell gift to my juniors.

434
00:28:06,918 --> 00:28:08,720
Please don't say that, Dr. Busujima.

435
00:28:11,122 --> 00:28:15,060
My life will lead to
the future of many patients.

436
00:28:15,593 --> 00:28:16,761
Dr. Busujima.

437
00:28:19,564 --> 00:28:21,933
I want to ask you...

438
00:28:23,401 --> 00:28:24,636
What is it?

439
00:28:25,837 --> 00:28:28,039
Would you transfer to
a different hospital?

440
00:28:30,942 --> 00:28:33,278
What do you mean by that?

441
00:28:34,979 --> 00:28:39,451
We cannot let someone who has contributed
greatly to medical services in Japan

442
00:28:39,884 --> 00:28:44,823
die at Japan's greatest hospital,
built by the government.

443
00:28:46,291 --> 00:28:51,463
Are you asking me to die
at some other hospital?

444
00:28:54,265 --> 00:28:55,433
Please understand.

445
00:29:05,810 --> 00:29:10,582
Ms. Daimon. I don't like you.

446
00:29:11,983 --> 00:29:16,121
You disturbed the organization, and did
many operations for a ridiculous fee.

447
00:29:17,655 --> 00:29:21,860
Thanks to you, my husband
was fired from the hospital.

448
00:29:25,597 --> 00:29:29,601
Is my husband that sick?

449
00:29:31,636 --> 00:29:32,504
Yes.

450
00:29:34,005 --> 00:29:34,839
I thought so.

451
00:29:36,474 --> 00:29:41,112
But he said he wants to die
at that hospital for his juniors.

452
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:43,281
How stupid.

453
00:29:48,920 --> 00:29:52,323
May I help the two of you?

454
00:29:52,390 --> 00:29:54,058
As you said,

455
00:29:54,526 --> 00:29:56,427
Dr. Busujima is our senior.

456
00:29:57,228 --> 00:29:59,297
We cannot abandon him.

457
00:30:00,165 --> 00:30:01,966
What do you want me to do?

458
00:30:03,735 --> 00:30:06,538
We'd like your help for the operation.

459
00:30:08,273 --> 00:30:09,741
We'll be in charge of the liver.

460
00:30:10,408 --> 00:30:13,545
We'd like you to operate on the heart.

461
00:30:14,445 --> 00:30:17,749
East and west will cooperate
for a joint operation?

462
00:30:17,816 --> 00:30:19,851
Removing both the tumors at once

463
00:30:20,251 --> 00:30:23,154
is the only way to save Dr. Busujima.

464
00:30:24,722 --> 00:30:25,723
Please.

465
00:30:27,692 --> 00:30:29,894
I see.

466
00:30:31,796 --> 00:30:36,601
So your plan is to split
the responsibility of failure too.

467
00:30:37,235 --> 00:30:39,003
How dare you say such a thing!

468
00:30:39,938 --> 00:30:43,474
What's wrong with him? He's unbelievable.

469
00:30:43,541 --> 00:30:44,676
Dr. Ebina.

470
00:30:45,310 --> 00:30:47,512
- What's wrong?
- Dr. Busujima's condition

471
00:30:47,579 --> 00:30:48,713
has suddenly worsened.

472
00:30:50,782 --> 00:30:55,320
I still want to go on
lots of trips with my husband.

473
00:30:55,386 --> 00:30:57,121
Forty years.

474
00:30:57,689 --> 00:31:00,992
It's been forty years
and I know nothing about him.

475
00:31:03,194 --> 00:31:06,998
You don't make mistakes?

476
00:31:10,501 --> 00:31:11,369
That's right.

477
00:31:12,837 --> 00:31:15,440
I'll persuade my husband.

478
00:31:16,207 --> 00:31:20,044
When it comes to the surgery,
can I have you do it?

479
00:31:20,912 --> 00:31:22,046
- Yes.
- It's a promise.

480
00:31:23,681 --> 00:31:25,350
Then listen to my wish too.

481
00:31:25,416 --> 00:31:26,351
What is it?

482
00:31:26,417 --> 00:31:29,220
Next time you go on a trip,
tell me where you're going.

483
00:31:29,287 --> 00:31:32,957
- I don't want to run into you guys again.
- Fine.

484
00:31:37,095 --> 00:31:37,929
It's the hospital.

485
00:31:39,430 --> 00:31:41,566
Hello, this is Busujima.

486
00:31:53,778 --> 00:31:54,812
This is bad.

487
00:31:56,547 --> 00:31:57,615
We have to do it.

488
00:31:58,683 --> 00:32:00,318
Let's do it ourselves, Dr. Ebina.

489
00:32:01,486 --> 00:32:02,387
We're taking him.

490
00:32:03,855 --> 00:32:05,623
- The anesthetist?
- I contacted them.

491
00:32:05,690 --> 00:32:07,058
- Let's hurry.
- Yes.

492
00:32:19,203 --> 00:32:20,204
The liver first.

493
00:32:20,605 --> 00:32:21,439
Yes.

494
00:32:24,175 --> 00:32:25,610
What are you doing?

495
00:32:26,644 --> 00:32:29,314
We can't wait.
We'll have an emergency operation.

496
00:32:29,380 --> 00:32:30,615
I will not allow it.

497
00:32:33,918 --> 00:32:37,622
Do not jump into an operation
that could fail.

498
00:32:38,656 --> 00:32:42,226
One failure will ruin everything.

499
00:32:43,628 --> 00:32:48,633
That means the reputation
of this hospital that I've built

500
00:32:50,335 --> 00:32:55,707
will be ruined in a flash
by your selfish act.

501
00:32:56,140 --> 00:32:58,142
We won't know if we don't try.

502
00:32:59,978 --> 00:33:01,646
You want to get demoted again?

503
00:33:04,415 --> 00:33:07,719
I repeat. I will not allow the operation.

504
00:33:07,785 --> 00:33:10,121
I will allow the operation.

505
00:33:11,789 --> 00:33:12,690
Board Member Tendo.

506
00:33:12,757 --> 00:33:15,093
It's been a while, President Kurobe.

507
00:33:16,661 --> 00:33:21,632
What sort of authority
do you have to allow the operation?

508
00:33:22,066 --> 00:33:23,968
It's not a matter of authority.

509
00:33:24,936 --> 00:33:26,137
It's a matter of life.

510
00:33:27,438 --> 00:33:28,740
Unbelievable.

511
00:33:30,541 --> 00:33:32,543
I'm the head of this hospital.

512
00:33:32,610 --> 00:33:36,280
President Kurobe, if you're a doctor too,

513
00:33:37,248 --> 00:33:40,685
you should obsess over the life
that's in front of your eyes.

514
00:33:49,127 --> 00:33:50,194
- Let's begin.
- Yes.

515
00:34:08,112 --> 00:34:11,716
We'll now perform the liver's
S5 subsegmental resection.

516
00:34:11,783 --> 00:34:12,850
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

517
00:34:26,197 --> 00:34:27,131
- Monopolar.
- Yes.

518
00:34:31,536 --> 00:34:33,471
- Abdominal dropsy.
- Here.

519
00:34:42,146 --> 00:34:43,047
Suction.

520
00:34:43,114 --> 00:34:44,449
PERITONEAL DISSEMINATION

521
00:34:44,515 --> 00:34:46,584
The ruptured hepatocyte has spread.

522
00:34:48,352 --> 00:34:49,253
Dr. Ebina.

523
00:34:51,789 --> 00:34:53,524
I didn't think it was so advanced.

524
00:34:53,591 --> 00:34:55,092
It seems that...

525
00:34:55,159 --> 00:34:57,528
The people of the east are done for.

526
00:34:57,595 --> 00:35:01,699
At this rate, you and I are done for too.

527
00:35:04,202 --> 00:35:06,938
- Say it's inoperable.
- That's the best thing to do.

528
00:35:07,972 --> 00:35:11,342
Right now, we can say
that we didn't make it in time.

529
00:35:11,776 --> 00:35:13,644
But...

530
00:35:13,711 --> 00:35:14,979
Close him up.

531
00:35:26,924 --> 00:35:28,025
Kaji.

532
00:35:28,092 --> 00:35:28,926
Yes.

533
00:35:30,228 --> 00:35:33,998
It was short, but
it was nice working with you.

534
00:35:36,634 --> 00:35:37,535
We'll get demoted.

535
00:35:39,437 --> 00:35:40,571
- So?
- Let's do it.

536
00:35:40,638 --> 00:35:41,806
Inoperable.

537
00:35:47,712 --> 00:35:48,746
Don't close him up.

538
00:35:51,883 --> 00:35:52,917
Who is that?

539
00:35:53,518 --> 00:35:54,485
Demon?

540
00:35:59,790 --> 00:36:00,858
I knew it.

541
00:36:01,259 --> 00:36:02,293
You knew?

542
00:36:03,361 --> 00:36:06,164
I told you. He's my patient.

543
00:36:07,031 --> 00:36:08,166
Move.

544
00:36:08,232 --> 00:36:10,201
Sorry, you too.

545
00:36:11,469 --> 00:36:14,705
Vitals. Blood pressure 80.
Pulse 90, sinus.

546
00:36:14,772 --> 00:36:15,640
Got it.

547
00:36:15,706 --> 00:36:16,941
Let's begin.

548
00:36:17,275 --> 00:36:18,809
Total peritoneal resection.

549
00:36:18,876 --> 00:36:20,144
You, suction.

550
00:36:20,578 --> 00:36:22,146
You, hold this.

551
00:36:23,014 --> 00:36:23,881
- Metzenbaum.
- Yes.

552
00:36:27,618 --> 00:36:28,853
Perfect.

553
00:36:39,063 --> 00:36:39,964
Amazing.

554
00:36:40,331 --> 00:36:41,265
So fast.

555
00:36:42,133 --> 00:36:43,401
- Monopolar.
- Yes.

556
00:37:00,551 --> 00:37:01,752
The liver's done.

557
00:37:02,320 --> 00:37:05,489
- Get that tissue examined.
- Yes.

558
00:37:05,556 --> 00:37:06,524
We'll do the heart...

559
00:37:12,797 --> 00:37:14,599
Cardiac arrest. VF.

560
00:37:28,846 --> 00:37:29,747
Something's there.

561
00:37:32,917 --> 00:37:34,418
Resuscitate.

562
00:37:34,485 --> 00:37:35,853
- Administer epinephrine.
- Yes.

563
00:37:36,354 --> 00:37:37,455
Don't move his heart.

564
00:37:39,257 --> 00:37:40,157
What?

565
00:37:40,591 --> 00:37:41,525
Expose his carotid.

566
00:37:41,592 --> 00:37:43,094
His heart's stopped.

567
00:37:45,496 --> 00:37:47,865
What is that woman talking about?

568
00:37:48,299 --> 00:37:51,535
She realized the danger
of the carotid bursting.

569
00:37:51,602 --> 00:37:55,072
If the heart starts to move
right now, ruptured aneurysm

570
00:37:55,139 --> 00:37:57,441
might occur from a carotid artery
dissection.

571
00:37:57,942 --> 00:38:01,345
Block the carotid and bypass.
I'll resuscitate within 3 minutes.

572
00:38:01,412 --> 00:38:02,647
Impossible.

573
00:38:03,981 --> 00:38:05,349
2 minutes 40 seconds left.

574
00:38:05,416 --> 00:38:06,517
Disinfect the drape.

575
00:38:21,699 --> 00:38:23,668
Dr. Sasaki, handle anesthetics.

576
00:38:23,734 --> 00:38:25,036
Yawara, the drape.

577
00:38:25,102 --> 00:38:26,437
Hashimi, loupe.

578
00:38:32,543 --> 00:38:34,178
- Get ready.
- Yes.

579
00:38:34,612 --> 00:38:36,113
Please.

580
00:38:36,881 --> 00:38:38,115
Add 4 more units.

581
00:38:38,549 --> 00:38:39,884
- Yes.
- Please.

582
00:38:39,950 --> 00:38:40,985
Here's the loupe.

583
00:38:41,052 --> 00:38:42,119
Do not do anything.

584
00:38:42,853 --> 00:38:43,954
All of you, get out.

585
00:38:54,098 --> 00:38:55,132
They're leaving?

586
00:38:56,701 --> 00:38:57,968
Bring my loupe down.

587
00:38:58,035 --> 00:38:58,869
Okay.

588
00:39:00,071 --> 00:39:00,905
Thank you.

589
00:39:04,008 --> 00:39:07,311
Have that woman take full responsibility.

590
00:39:08,012 --> 00:39:11,048
Ebina, you guys
will not be held responsible.

591
00:39:11,415 --> 00:39:12,650
It's the best thing to do.

592
00:39:17,822 --> 00:39:18,889
Dr. Ebina.

593
00:39:26,430 --> 00:39:28,199
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir?

594
00:39:28,265 --> 00:39:29,967
Everyone, leave.

595
00:39:43,314 --> 00:39:45,349
It ends up like this no matter where I go.

596
00:39:46,250 --> 00:39:48,619
- Maybe because you're involved.
- What?

597
00:39:49,387 --> 00:39:51,689
- 1 minute 50 seconds left.
- Roger.

598
00:39:53,224 --> 00:39:55,025
You stop too, part-timer.

599
00:39:55,092 --> 00:39:55,926
Stop.

600
00:39:55,993 --> 00:39:57,027
I won't do that.

601
00:39:57,094 --> 00:40:00,431
You're going to fail, anyway.

602
00:40:00,498 --> 00:40:01,632
Stop it.

603
00:40:05,102 --> 00:40:07,772
I don't make mistakes.

604
00:40:09,073 --> 00:40:09,907
What?

605
00:40:20,718 --> 00:40:22,086
Carotid blocked off.

606
00:40:22,153 --> 00:40:22,987
Shunt tube.

607
00:40:23,521 --> 00:40:25,289
I don't think they have it.

608
00:40:25,689 --> 00:40:26,557
What?

609
00:40:44,475 --> 00:40:47,077
- I've brought the shunt tube.
- Thank you.

610
00:40:47,144 --> 00:40:49,346
- Hashiguchi, be ready to assist.
- Yes.

611
00:40:49,413 --> 00:40:50,981
- Manabe, assist her.
- Yes.

612
00:40:51,048 --> 00:40:51,982
- And you.
- Yes.

613
00:40:53,884 --> 00:40:54,852
45 seconds left.

614
00:40:54,919 --> 00:40:56,253
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

615
00:40:59,423 --> 00:41:00,391
- Potts.
- Yes.

616
00:41:05,429 --> 00:41:07,298
- Insert shunt tube.
- Yes.

617
00:41:15,639 --> 00:41:17,074
- Vascular clamp.
- Yes.

618
00:41:24,615 --> 00:41:26,016
Shunt complete.

619
00:41:26,083 --> 00:41:26,984
15 seconds.

620
00:41:27,518 --> 00:41:29,019
- Charge DC.
- Yes.

621
00:41:34,859 --> 00:41:35,759
Here you are.

622
00:41:40,297 --> 00:41:41,131
Stay back.

623
00:42:00,551 --> 00:42:04,321
Pulse is back. The heart was stopped
for 2 minutes 58 seconds.

624
00:42:04,722 --> 00:42:06,190
Administering epinephrine.

625
00:42:06,257 --> 00:42:08,926
- Vitals?
- Blood pressure 70s. Pulse 50s.

626
00:42:08,993 --> 00:42:10,094
It's improving.

627
00:42:11,061 --> 00:42:12,429
Aneurysm resection,

628
00:42:12,496 --> 00:42:14,598
and we'll remove the
heart tumor after that.

629
00:42:14,665 --> 00:42:15,533
Yes.

630
00:42:26,810 --> 00:42:29,146
That woman is unbelievable.

631
00:42:29,213 --> 00:42:31,882
Is she really a part-timer?

632
00:42:33,350 --> 00:42:38,822
Heart, liver, and carotid.
She's doing three parts simultaneously.

633
00:42:39,757 --> 00:42:43,093
She really is a thousand-hand goddess.

634
00:42:53,704 --> 00:42:55,573
1,300cc of blood loss.

635
00:42:56,006 --> 00:42:56,941
Vitals are normal.

636
00:42:57,942 --> 00:42:59,109
Done.

637
00:42:59,843 --> 00:43:00,978
Thank you.

638
00:43:01,412 --> 00:43:02,746
Thank you.

639
00:43:07,651 --> 00:43:10,254
Use your life for your own good.

640
00:43:13,057 --> 00:43:15,559
You sure do worry us.

641
00:43:15,893 --> 00:43:17,161
Good job.

642
00:43:17,227 --> 00:43:18,128
Well done.

643
00:43:29,406 --> 00:43:30,341
Excuse me.

644
00:43:32,876 --> 00:43:34,945
I brought Michiko Daimon's resume.

645
00:43:38,816 --> 00:43:45,189
Army surgeon? Ship doctor.
Veterinarian. Emergency doctor.

646
00:43:45,789 --> 00:43:49,326
Only at resort areas.

647
00:43:51,028 --> 00:43:52,129
Ridiculous.

648
00:43:58,535 --> 00:43:59,403
Here you are.

649
00:43:59,903 --> 00:44:00,738
Thank you.

650
00:44:03,440 --> 00:44:05,442
Hobbies: surgery.

651
00:44:05,509 --> 00:44:08,345
Talents: surgery.

652
00:44:17,888 --> 00:44:22,493
Wait until next year for a vacation.

653
00:44:24,561 --> 00:44:26,030
Ms. Daimon.

654
00:44:32,002 --> 00:44:34,038
Thank you.

655
00:44:59,930 --> 00:45:02,833
You guys saved me.

656
00:45:04,134 --> 00:45:06,637
You shouldn't be too brash.

657
00:45:07,304 --> 00:45:08,338
What?

658
00:45:08,405 --> 00:45:11,208
It's bad enough with
the east and west thing.

659
00:45:11,709 --> 00:45:14,445
Don't worry.
That was my only surgery here.

660
00:45:14,511 --> 00:45:16,847
Then I'll give you advice
for your future career.

661
00:45:17,781 --> 00:45:19,083
Don't get the wrong idea.

662
00:45:20,284 --> 00:45:22,920
- Okay?
- There are no doctors who don't fail.

663
00:45:27,458 --> 00:45:31,261
A super doctor like you
is the biggest nuisance for us.

664
00:45:35,766 --> 00:45:42,272
All the nurses who disobeyed me and
participated in the surgery are fired.

665
00:45:42,339 --> 00:45:46,510
Dr. Busujima's operation
was successfully carried out by

666
00:45:46,577 --> 00:45:53,183
a joint effort by Ebina of the east
and Dangozaka of the west.

667
00:45:54,251 --> 00:45:55,753
How's that?

668
00:45:55,819 --> 00:45:56,887
That's great.

669
00:45:56,954 --> 00:45:59,857
The reputation of this hospital
will go up again.

670
00:46:00,424 --> 00:46:02,059
Your reputation as well?

671
00:46:02,126 --> 00:46:04,995
Mr. Tendo,

672
00:46:05,329 --> 00:46:07,064
how mean of you.

673
00:46:08,065 --> 00:46:11,802
But not anymore.

674
00:46:14,505 --> 00:46:15,439
Ikawa.

675
00:46:15,506 --> 00:46:16,373
Yes.

676
00:46:20,811 --> 00:46:21,812
Here you are.

677
00:46:27,050 --> 00:46:30,687
(Tetsuya Kurobe, Dismissed)

678
00:46:31,221 --> 00:46:32,055
What is this?

679
00:46:32,122 --> 00:46:35,559
I should've shown you
before the operation.

680
00:46:35,626 --> 00:46:37,995
This can't be.

681
00:46:38,061 --> 00:46:40,531
I will not accept this.

682
00:46:41,031 --> 00:46:43,100
It's a decision made
by the board of directors.

683
00:46:44,168 --> 00:46:46,503
There are no more
board members or contractors

684
00:46:46,570 --> 00:46:49,173
who'll be feeding you manju.

685
00:46:51,809 --> 00:46:52,876
Excuse me.

686
00:46:52,943 --> 00:46:54,311
Who are you?

687
00:46:54,378 --> 00:46:58,715
Thank you very much for
using our Michiko Daimon.

688
00:46:59,316 --> 00:47:04,621
Who should I give the bill to,
for Dr. Busujima's surgery?

689
00:47:04,688 --> 00:47:06,056
I'll take it,

690
00:47:06,990 --> 00:47:09,526
since I'll be the next president.

691
00:47:13,630 --> 00:47:14,865
APPOINTMENT

692
00:47:14,932 --> 00:47:17,501
YOSHIHITO TENDO AS PRESIDENT

693
00:47:17,568 --> 00:47:20,470
Tendo?

694
00:47:21,305 --> 00:47:22,406
What a surprise!

695
00:47:22,906 --> 00:47:24,675
Congratulations.

696
00:47:27,744 --> 00:47:28,779
This is a melon.

697
00:47:29,346 --> 00:47:30,280
This is a bill.

698
00:47:37,221 --> 00:47:38,488
I see.

699
00:47:38,555 --> 00:47:42,292
Ten million yen?
What is this ridiculous price?

700
00:47:42,359 --> 00:47:47,231
Superb technique calls for
a suitable price. It's market price.

701
00:47:47,764 --> 00:47:49,032
I understand.

702
00:47:59,042 --> 00:48:00,410
Cash.

703
00:48:01,345 --> 00:48:02,946
Thank you very much.

704
00:48:05,949 --> 00:48:06,783
Here you are.

705
00:48:08,352 --> 00:48:10,454
This is not enough.

706
00:48:10,520 --> 00:48:12,155
It's for your cab ride.

707
00:48:12,956 --> 00:48:15,692
We'll wire your money
to your account later.

708
00:48:17,127 --> 00:48:20,364
This is for ex-president Kurobe.

709
00:48:24,067 --> 00:48:25,569
A farewell gift.

710
00:48:28,639 --> 00:48:31,975
Is there manju under the melon?

711
00:48:32,042 --> 00:48:33,176
No.

712
00:48:36,446 --> 00:48:37,281
I don't want it.

713
00:48:48,892 --> 00:48:53,330
What? Like this, like this...

714
00:48:53,764 --> 00:48:56,733
Like this, like this...

715
00:48:57,100 --> 00:49:00,237
I can do it.

716
00:49:02,172 --> 00:49:06,677
I gave you lots of trouble.

717
00:49:07,210 --> 00:49:11,581
Who performed the surgery?

718
00:49:12,449 --> 00:49:17,587
Ebina, of Totei University.

719
00:49:19,189 --> 00:49:20,023
Welll...

720
00:49:20,090 --> 00:49:23,694
Dr. Busujima, you have
quite a talented junior.

721
00:49:23,760 --> 00:49:25,295
I'm jealous.

722
00:49:26,196 --> 00:49:30,634
As a result, we'll be able to
give the world's first case report...

723
00:49:30,701 --> 00:49:34,204
Just as you wished.

724
00:49:34,271 --> 00:49:36,239
- World's first?
- I see.

725
00:49:36,807 --> 00:49:41,111
Dr. Ebina, please write
the case report immediately.

726
00:49:41,778 --> 00:49:43,847
Yes. Excuse me.

727
00:49:49,853 --> 00:49:51,488
World's first.

728
00:49:53,590 --> 00:49:54,624
So lucky.

729
00:50:01,131 --> 00:50:06,470
You did a great job in the end too.

730
00:50:07,471 --> 00:50:14,444
Are you telling me to
cut all ties with this hospital?

731
00:50:16,813 --> 00:50:18,415
Of course not.

732
00:50:21,018 --> 00:50:25,856
It means I got a nice gift.

733
00:50:27,424 --> 00:50:28,258
What?

734
00:50:29,459 --> 00:50:33,230
Doctor X. A wonderful surgeon.

735
00:50:35,632 --> 00:50:37,300
Thank you very much.

736
00:50:53,250 --> 00:50:54,951
Akira.

737
00:50:55,018 --> 00:50:58,355
Who am I supposed to take
the bill for Busujima's surgery to?

738
00:50:58,422 --> 00:51:02,759
Oh, I forgot about that.

739
00:51:03,794 --> 00:51:07,731
It was Busujima's wife
that asked me to operate,

740
00:51:08,331 --> 00:51:11,234
but maybe the bill should
go to that nasty Kuro...

741
00:51:11,802 --> 00:51:13,236
Kurobe, the president.

742
00:51:13,303 --> 00:51:16,907
What are you talking about?
We can't a send a bill anywhere.

743
00:51:17,741 --> 00:51:18,775
Why?

744
00:51:18,842 --> 00:51:22,612
Because you just
ran out on your own and did it.

745
00:51:24,815 --> 00:51:27,284
This is the only free service.

746
00:51:27,684 --> 00:51:32,155
Starting next time,
you'll be working very hard.

747
00:51:33,490 --> 00:51:34,391
Seriously?

748
00:51:34,458 --> 00:51:36,560
Seriously.

749
00:51:36,626 --> 00:51:38,628
Seriously?

750
00:51:40,230 --> 00:51:41,131
Quiet.

751
00:51:41,631 --> 00:51:42,532
Quiet.

752
00:51:43,567 --> 00:51:44,534
Now,

753
00:51:45,001 --> 00:51:51,908
I'd like to have a word
from Mr. Tendo, the new president.

754
00:51:53,076 --> 00:51:55,378
I know,

755
00:51:56,179 --> 00:52:00,250
there is a meaningless
power struggle in this hospital.

756
00:52:00,917 --> 00:52:06,323
That is because you have forgotten
the true mission of this hospital.

757
00:52:06,790 --> 00:52:12,829
The true mission of this hospital
is "From labor to leader."

758
00:52:13,997 --> 00:52:17,767
In order to carry out the world's
leading research and clinical medicine,

759
00:52:18,235 --> 00:52:24,074
I would like to call for reform.

760
00:52:24,141 --> 00:52:25,709
Reform?

761
00:52:25,775 --> 00:52:26,843
First,

762
00:52:27,844 --> 00:52:31,047
abolish the medical office
of the east and west wards.

763
00:52:31,882 --> 00:52:35,318
We'll unify the medical office
from both sides,

764
00:52:35,385 --> 00:52:38,288
as a strategically integrated
surgical department.

765
00:52:38,355 --> 00:52:39,489
Strategy?

766
00:52:40,991 --> 00:52:43,226
That's impossible.

767
00:52:43,627 --> 00:52:44,728
It is.

768
00:52:44,794 --> 00:52:45,795
Second,

769
00:52:47,130 --> 00:52:49,266
the integration of each manager's office.

770
00:52:50,634 --> 00:52:55,972
We'll combine the two managers'
offices in the east and west ward.

771
00:52:56,406 --> 00:52:59,176
- My castle will disappear?
- Then who's the manager?

772
00:53:00,243 --> 00:53:03,947
Third, scouting new personnel.

773
00:53:05,282 --> 00:53:09,653
We have already signed
a contract with a surgeon.

774
00:53:11,188 --> 00:53:12,856
A contract? No way.

775
00:53:12,923 --> 00:53:13,857
Please come in.

776
00:53:19,863 --> 00:53:21,531
I knew it, Demon.

777
00:53:21,932 --> 00:53:28,471
President Tendo, thank you for signing
a contract with our Michiko Daimon.

778
00:53:28,939 --> 00:53:30,774
This is Dr. Michiko Daimon.

779
00:53:31,741 --> 00:53:34,511
She graduated from the medical
department of Totei University

780
00:53:34,578 --> 00:53:36,713
with excellent grades.

781
00:53:36,780 --> 00:53:40,250
Then, she went to a battlefield
and acted as an army surgeon...

782
00:53:40,317 --> 00:53:41,151
No need for that.

783
00:53:45,922 --> 00:53:51,294
Now that we've signed the contract, these
are the terms I'd like for you to follow.

784
00:53:59,369 --> 00:54:00,537
What is this?

785
00:54:00,971 --> 00:54:03,673
I told you. Working conditions.

786
00:54:04,741 --> 00:54:06,943
I will read it now.

787
00:54:07,010 --> 00:54:08,044
For example,

788
00:54:08,445 --> 00:54:10,380
- thesis research.
- I won't do that.

789
00:54:10,447 --> 00:54:12,315
- Go to academic meetings.
- I won't.

790
00:54:12,382 --> 00:54:14,584
- Being a chauffeur for golf.
- I won't.

791
00:54:14,651 --> 00:54:17,020
- Helping to hide a lover.
- I won't.

792
00:54:17,087 --> 00:54:19,089
- Helping out for promotion.
- I won't.

793
00:54:19,155 --> 00:54:23,026
- Support for power struggle.
- I absolutely won't do that.

794
00:54:23,093 --> 00:54:23,994
Et cetera.

795
00:54:25,228 --> 00:54:27,731
I will not do work that can be done

796
00:54:27,797 --> 00:54:29,199
without a medical license.

797
00:54:32,469 --> 00:54:36,072
And so, we look forward
to working with you.

798
00:54:37,207 --> 00:54:38,875
This is deja vu.

799
00:54:38,942 --> 00:54:40,410
I see.

800
00:54:40,477 --> 00:54:44,447
Everything written here is only natural.

801
00:54:44,914 --> 00:54:48,852
You didn't have to write it
in the contract.

802
00:54:50,654 --> 00:54:54,758
Everybody. I have one last thing to say.

803
00:54:55,759 --> 00:54:57,093
- Ikawa.
- Yes.

804
00:55:04,634 --> 00:55:05,602
What is this?

805
00:55:06,136 --> 00:55:07,337
I don't understand.

806
00:55:11,174 --> 00:55:12,676
It's a letter of resignation.

807
00:55:13,677 --> 00:55:16,012
I'd like for you to sign it right now.

808
00:55:16,713 --> 00:55:18,381
Do not write a date.

809
00:55:18,448 --> 00:55:20,684
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

810
00:55:24,154 --> 00:55:26,923
- Why?
- Why a letter of resignation?

811
00:55:29,592 --> 00:55:31,761
He wants us to entrust our lives to him?

812
00:55:45,709 --> 00:55:47,310
Honey, what should I do?

813
00:55:52,015 --> 00:55:53,717
She signed it.

814
00:56:01,558 --> 00:56:04,894
I WON'T DO THAT

815
00:56:04,961 --> 00:56:07,664
You think I'd give a resignation
the day I was hired?

816
00:56:28,551 --> 00:56:29,452
What's going on?

817
00:56:29,519 --> 00:56:31,121
We're being tested?

818
00:56:32,455 --> 00:56:33,356
How scary.

819
00:56:36,559 --> 00:56:41,131
Dr. Daimon. I took a look at your resume.

820
00:56:41,698 --> 00:56:47,137
Hobby: surgery. Talents: surgery.
You have others.

821
00:56:47,203 --> 00:56:51,508
Mahjong, horseracing, going to clubs,
public baths, table tennis,

822
00:56:51,574 --> 00:56:53,143
and tuna auctions.

823
00:56:54,110 --> 00:56:56,413
You sure have a lot of hobbies.

824
00:56:57,414 --> 00:56:59,616
Why do you know about my private life?

825
00:57:00,517 --> 00:57:04,020
From now on,
please be of use to this hospital.

826
00:57:09,225 --> 00:57:10,827
I look forward to working with you.

827
00:57:12,061 --> 00:57:15,231
You can do that without a medical license.

828
00:57:18,067 --> 00:57:19,135
Bye.

829
00:57:20,670 --> 00:57:21,905
I'll be leaving too.

830
00:57:42,325 --> 00:57:45,862
Tendo is the president?

831
00:57:45,929 --> 00:57:47,864
Are you crazy?

832
00:57:50,233 --> 00:57:51,134
That means...

833
00:57:51,701 --> 00:57:55,138
The poison manju didn't work?

834
00:57:55,205 --> 00:57:56,239
No.

835
00:57:56,306 --> 00:58:01,211
Then start crushing
all the guys of the east.

836
00:58:01,878 --> 00:58:02,545
Yes.

837
00:58:02,612 --> 00:58:04,881
First, Michiko Daimon.

838
00:58:04,948 --> 00:58:05,782
Yes.

839
00:58:05,849 --> 00:58:10,420
As long as she's around,
the west will not gain control.

840
00:58:10,887 --> 00:58:12,455
- Yes.
- Are you listening?

841
00:58:12,922 --> 00:58:14,557
- Yes, sir.
- Dango.

842
00:58:14,624 --> 00:58:15,859
Yes, sir.

843
00:58:16,526 --> 00:58:17,494
<i>Dango.</i>

844
00:58:19,128 --> 00:58:21,431
<i>Michiko Daimon.</i>

845
00:58:35,478 --> 00:58:39,249
<i>She despises teams, authority</i>
<i>and the restraints they bring.</i>

846
00:58:39,315 --> 00:58:43,520
<i>Her license and the skills she has</i>
<i>earned are her only weapons.</i>

847
00:58:44,821 --> 00:58:47,290
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

848
00:58:47,357 --> 00:58:50,760
<i>also known as Doctor-X.</i>

849
01:00:09,205 --> 01:00:11,874
If we kill the world's smartest brain,
this hospital is done.

850
01:00:11,941 --> 01:00:13,543
This is a national crisis.

851
01:00:13,610 --> 01:00:17,213
My hands are much more skilled
and accurate than a robot's.

852
01:00:17,280 --> 01:00:20,049
I know. You killed a man.

853
01:00:20,116 --> 01:00:21,985
Can you do this operation?

854
01:00:22,051 --> 01:00:23,419
Change the patient.
